IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp1-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division A -- sections 5, 6 and 7: THE MINISTER, PENSIONABLE EMPLOYMENT AND
-- EXCEPTED EMPLOYMENT.
--
-- Section 5 names the Minister (National Revenue, which the keel's `Minister` type already carries) and lets the
-- Minister delegate. Section 6 says which employment is pensionable (the employment on which contributions are
-- made) and which is excepted. Section 7 lets the Governor in Council extend or narrow both by regulation; the
-- regulation-making powers are machinery (NOTES.md, coverage table), but the limitation in subsection 7(4) says
-- what a regulation may not do to a foreign government or an international organization and is encoded.
--
-- A regulation made under section 7 is in Part III of the Regulations (piece cr1): whether one includes or
-- excepts an employment is a plain input here, never worked out.

§ `Division A -- Contributions Payable`

§§ `Section 5 -- the Minister and delegation`

-- src:123 | Definition of Minister
-- src:124 | 5 (1) In this Part, Minister means the Minister of National Revenue.
@ref Act s 5(1) (src:123-124)
GIVETH A Minister
`s 5(1) — the Minister for Part I` MEANS `the Minister of National Revenue`

-- src:125 | Delegation
-- src:126 | (2) The Minister may authorize an officer or a class of officers to exercise powers or perform duties of the Minister under this Part.
@ref Act s 5(2) (src:125-126)
GIVEN `the Minister has authorized the officer, or a class of officers that includes the officer, to exercise the power or perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(2) — an officer may exercise a power or perform a duty of the Minister under Part I` `the Minister has authorized the officer, or a class of officers that includes the officer, to exercise the power or perform the duty` MEANS
    `the Minister has authorized the officer, or a class of officers that includes the officer, to exercise the power or perform the duty`

§§ `Section 6 -- pensionable employment and excepted employment`

-- Excepted employment is dealt with first, because paragraphs 6(1)(a) and (b) are defined by what it is not.

-- src:136 | Excepted employment
-- src:137 | (2) Excepted employment is
-- src:138 | (a) employment in agriculture or an agricultural enterprise, horticulture, fishing, hunting, trapping, forestry, logging or lumbering by an employer who either pays the employee less than two hundred and fifty dollars in cash remuneration in a year or employs the employee, on terms providing for payment of cash remuneration, for a period of less than twenty-five working days in a year;
@ref Act s 6(2)(a) (src:138)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(2)(a) — the employment is excepted employment in agriculture and the like` employment MEANS
        employment's `the employment is in agriculture or an agricultural enterprise, horticulture, fishing, hunting, trapping, forestry, logging or lumbering`
    AND (    employment's `cash remuneration the employer pays the employee in the year` LESS THAN 250
          OR (    employment's `the employer employs the employee on terms providing for payment of cash remuneration`
              AND employment's `working days in the year for which the employer so employs the employee` LESS THAN 25))

-- src:139 | (b) employment of a casual nature otherwise than for the purpose of the employer’s trade or business;
@ref Act s 6(2)(b) (src:139)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(2)(b) — the employment is excepted employment of a casual nature outside the employer's business` employment MEANS
        employment's `the employment is of a casual nature`
    AND (NOT employment's `the employment is for the purpose of the employer's trade or business`)

-- src:140 | (c) employment as a teacher on exchange from a country other than Canada;
@ref Act s 6(2)(c) (src:140)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(2)(c) — the employment is excepted employment as a teacher on exchange` employment MEANS
    employment's `the employee is a teacher on exchange from a country other than Canada`

-- src:141 | (d) employment of a person by the person’s spouse or common-law partner, unless the remuneration paid to the person may be deducted under the Income Tax Act in computing the income of the spouse or common-law partner;
@ref Act s 6(2)(d) (src:141)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(2)(d) — the employment is excepted employment by a spouse or common-law partner` employment MEANS
        employment's `the employee is employed by the employee's spouse or common-law partner`
    AND (NOT employment's `the remuneration paid may be deducted under the Income Tax Act in computing the income of the spouse or common-law partner`)

-- src:142 | (e) employment of a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of perpetual poverty and whose remuneration is paid either directly or by the member to the order;
@ref Act s 6(2)(e) (src:142)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(2)(e) — the employment is excepted employment of a member of a religious order` employment MEANS
        employment's `the employee is a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of perpetual poverty`
    AND employment's `the remuneration is paid either directly or by the member to the order`

-- src:143 | (f) employment for which no cash remuneration is paid where the person employed is the child of, or is maintained by, the employer;
@ref Act s 6(2)(f) (src:143)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(2)(f) — the employment is excepted employment without cash remuneration` employment MEANS
        employment's `no cash remuneration is paid`
    AND (    employment's `the employee is the child of the employer`
          OR employment's `the employee is maintained by the employer`)

-- src:144 | (g) employment as a member of the Canadian Forces or the Royal Canadian Mounted Police, except as provided by any other Act of Parliament;
@ref Act s 6(2)(g) (src:144)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(2)(g) — the employment is excepted employment in the Canadian Forces or the Royal Canadian Mounted Police` employment MEANS
        employment's `the employment is as a member of the Canadian Forces or the Royal Canadian Mounted Police`
    AND (NOT employment's `another Act of Parliament provides otherwise for that employment`)

-- src:145 | (h) employment in Canada by an employer who employs persons in Canada but under the terms of a reciprocal agreement between the Government of Canada and the government of another country is exempt from liability to make the contributions imposed on an employer by this Act;
@ref Act s 6(2)(h) (src:145)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(2)(h) — the employment is excepted employment under a reciprocal agreement` employment MEANS
        employment's `the employment is in Canada`
    AND employment's `the employer employs persons in Canada`
    AND employment's `a reciprocal agreement between the Government of Canada and the government of another country exempts the employer from liability to make the contributions imposed on an employer by this Act`

-- src:146 | (i) employment by Her Majesty in right of a province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province;
@ref Act s 6(2)(i) (src:146)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(2)(i) — the employment is excepted employment by Her Majesty in right of a province` employment MEANS
    employment's `the employment is by Her Majesty in right of a province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province`

-- src:147 | (j) employment in Canada by the government of a country other than Canada or by an international organization;
@ref Act s 6(2)(j) (src:147)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(2)(j) — the employment is excepted employment by a foreign government or an international organization` employment MEANS
        employment's `the employment is in Canada`
    AND employment's `the employment is by the government of a country other than Canada or by an international organization`

-- src:148 | (j.1) employment of an Indian, as defined in the Indian Act, in respect of which the earnings are not included in computing income for purposes of the Income Tax Act; or
@ref Act s 6(2)(j.1) (src:148)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(2)(j.1) — the employment is excepted employment of an Indian whose earnings are not income` employment MEANS
        employment's `the employee is an Indian as defined in the Indian Act`
    AND employment's `the earnings from the employment are not included in computing income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act`

-- src:149 | (k) employment excepted from pensionable employment by a regulation made under section 7.
@ref Act s 6(2)(k) (src:149)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(2)(k) — the employment is excepted by a regulation made under section 7` employment MEANS
    employment's `a regulation made under section 7 excepts the employment from pensionable employment`

-- Excepted employment is any of the eleven.
@ref Act s 6(2) (src:136-149)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(2) — the employment is excepted employment` employment MEANS
        `s 6(2)(a) — the employment is excepted employment in agriculture and the like` employment
    OR  `s 6(2)(b) — the employment is excepted employment of a casual nature outside the employer's business` employment
    OR  `s 6(2)(c) — the employment is excepted employment as a teacher on exchange` employment
    OR  `s 6(2)(d) — the employment is excepted employment by a spouse or common-law partner` employment
    OR  `s 6(2)(e) — the employment is excepted employment of a member of a religious order` employment
    OR  `s 6(2)(f) — the employment is excepted employment without cash remuneration` employment
    OR  `s 6(2)(g) — the employment is excepted employment in the Canadian Forces or the Royal Canadian Mounted Police` employment
    OR  `s 6(2)(h) — the employment is excepted employment under a reciprocal agreement` employment
    OR  `s 6(2)(i) — the employment is excepted employment by Her Majesty in right of a province` employment
    OR  `s 6(2)(j) — the employment is excepted employment by a foreign government or an international organization` employment
    OR  `s 6(2)(j.1) — the employment is excepted employment of an Indian whose earnings are not income` employment
    OR  `s 6(2)(k) — the employment is excepted by a regulation made under section 7` employment

-- src:131 | Pensionable employment
-- src:132 | 6 (1) Pensionable employment is
-- src:133 | (a) employment in Canada that is not excepted employment;
-- src:134 | (b) employment in Canada under Her Majesty in right of Canada that is not excepted employment; or
-- src:135 | (c) employment included in pensionable employment by a regulation made under section 7.
@ref Act s 6(1)(a) (src:133)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(1)(a) — the employment is employment in Canada that is not excepted employment` employment MEANS
        employment's `the employment is in Canada`
    AND (NOT `s 6(2) — the employment is excepted employment` employment)

@ref Act s 6(1)(b) (src:134)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(1)(b) — the employment is employment in Canada under Her Majesty in right of Canada that is not excepted employment` employment MEANS
        employment's `the employment is in Canada`
    AND employment's `the employment is under Her Majesty in right of Canada`
    AND (NOT `s 6(2) — the employment is excepted employment` employment)

@ref Act s 6(1)(c) (src:135)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(1)(c) — the employment is included in pensionable employment by a regulation made under section 7` employment MEANS
    employment's `a regulation made under section 7 includes the employment in pensionable employment`

-- Pensionable employment is any of the three.
@ref Act s 6(1) (src:131-135)
GIVEN employment IS A `cp1 Facts about an employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(1) — the employment is pensionable employment` employment MEANS
        `s 6(1)(a) — the employment is employment in Canada that is not excepted employment` employment
    OR  `s 6(1)(b) — the employment is employment in Canada under Her Majesty in right of Canada that is not excepted employment` employment
    OR  `s 6(1)(c) — the employment is included in pensionable employment by a regulation made under section 7` employment

§§ `Section 7 -- regulations about pensionable employment`

-- Subsections 7(1), 7(2) and 7(3) are powers of the Governor in Council to make regulations (including, excepting
-- and adapting employment): machinery, inert in NOTES.md. What the Governor in Council has done is read from
-- Part III of the Regulations (piece cr1), and enters this module only as the two regulation inputs of the
-- record `cp1 Facts about an employment`.

-- src:169 | Limitation
-- src:170 | (4) No regulation under this section shall require the payment of an employer’s contribution by the government of a country other than Canada or by an international organization unless the regulation is made pursuant to an agreement referred to in paragraph (1)(f).
@ref Act s 7(4) (src:169-170)
GIVEN `the regulation requires the payment of an employer's contribution by the government of a country other than Canada or by an international organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulation is made pursuant to an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 7(4) — a regulation under section 7 may require an employer's contribution from a foreign government or an international organization` `the regulation requires the payment of an employer's contribution by the government of a country other than Canada or by an international organization` `the regulation is made pursuant to an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(f)` MEANS
        (NOT `the regulation requires the payment of an employer's contribution by the government of a country other than Canada or by an international organization`)
    OR  `the regulation is made pursuant to an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(f)`
